Appendix B: Algorithm Specifications

B.1 Continuous-Discrete Extended Kalman Smoother (CDEKS)

Algorithm B.1 (CDEKS Forward Pass).

```
Input: Observations {Y_k}, intervention schedules {u_j(t)}, environmental conditions E(t),
       parameter estimates Θ = {A_0, A_j, C, Q, R}
Output: Filtered state estimates {X̂_k|k}, predicted state estimates {X̂_k|k-1},
        covariance matrices {P_k|k, P_k|k-1}

Initialize: X̂_0|0 = μ_0, P_0|0 = Σ_0

For k = 1, 2, ..., K:
    # Prediction step (continuous-time integration between observations)
    Δt_k = t_k - t_{k-1}
    Solve ODE: dX̂/dt = (A_0 + Σ_j u_j(t) A_j) X̂ + C E(t)  over [t_{k-1}, t_k]
    Solve Lyapunov: dP/dt = (A_0 + Σ_j u_j A_j)P + P(A_0 + Σ_j u_j A_j)^T + Q
    
    # Update step (only for observed variables)
    If H_k has nonzero entries:
        S_k = H_k P_k|k-1 H_k^T + R_k
        K_k = P_k|k-1 H_k^T S_k^{-1}
        X̂_k|k = X̂_k|k-1 + K_k (Y_k - H_k X̂_k|k-1)
        P_k|k = (I - K_k H_k) P_k|k-1
    Else:
        X̂_k|k = X̂_k|k-1
        P_k|k = P_k|k-1
```

Algorithm B.2 (CDEKS Backward Pass—Rauch-Tung-Striebel Smoother).

```
Input: Filtered estimates {X̂_k|k, P_k|k}, predicted estimates {X̂_k|k-1, P_k|k-1}
Output: Smoothed estimates {X̂_k|K, P_k|K}

Initialize: X̂_K|K, P_K|K from forward pass

For k = K-1, K-2, ..., 0:
    J_k = P_k|k (A_0 + Σ_j u_j(t_k) A_j)^T P_{k+1|k}^{-1}
    X̂_k|K = X̂_k|k + J_k (X̂_{k+1|K} - X̂_{k+1|k})
    P_k|K = P_k|k + J_k (P_{k+1|K} - P_{k+1|k}) J_k^T
```

B.2 Expectation-Maximization for CDEKS

Algorithm B.3 (EM Loop for Parameter Estimation).

```
Input: Observations {Y_k}, control schedules {u_j(t)}, initial parameters Θ^(0), 
       convergence tolerance ε = 1e-6, maximum iterations N_max = 500
Output: MLE parameters Θ^*

For r = 0, 1, 2, ..., N_max:
    # E-Step: Run CDEKS with current parameters
    {X̂_k|K, P_k|K, J_k} ← CDEKS(Y, u, E, Θ^(r))
    
    # M-Step: Update parameters
    # Update process noise covariance Q:
    Q^(r+1) = (1/K) Σ_k [ E[(X_k - F_{k-1}X_{k-1})(X_k - F_{k-1}X_{k-1})^T] ]
    
    # Update measurement noise covariance R:
    R^(r+1) = (1/K) Σ_k [ E[(Y_k - H_k X_k)(Y_k - H_k X_k)^T] ]
    
    # Update system matrices via gradient ascent on expected log-likelihood:
    A_0^(r+1) = A_0^(r) + η ∇_{A_0} Q(Θ; Θ^(r))
    A_j^(r+1) = A_j^(r) + η ∇_{A_j} Q(Θ; Θ^(r))
    C^(r+1) = C^(r) + η ∇_C Q(Θ; Θ^(r))
    
    # Check convergence:
    If |log-likelihood^(r+1) - log-likelihood^(r)| < ε:
        Return Θ^(r+1)
```

B.3 Hamilton-Jacobi-Bellman Equation Solver

Algorithm B.4 (Level-Set Method for Stochastic Viability HJB).

```
Input: System matrices {A_0, A_j}, noise covariance Q, constraint set K,
       time horizon T, grid resolution N per dimension, control grid {u^(l)}
Output: Viability value function v(x, t) on grid

# Discretize state space:
Grid G = {x_1^(i1), x_2^(i2), x_3^(i3), x_4^(i4)} for i_m = 1, ..., N

# Initialize terminal condition:
v(x, T) = 1{K}(x) = 1 if ℓ(x) ≥ 0, else 0

# Time-marching backward:
For t = T - Δt, T - 2Δt, ..., 0:
    # For each grid point:
    For each x ∈ G:
        # Compute Hamiltonian:
        For each control u^(l) ∈ U_grid:
            drift = (A_0 + Σ_j u_j^(l) A_j) x + C E(t)
            Hamiltonian^(l) = drift^T ∇_x v + 0.5 * Tr(Q ∇_x^2 v)
        H_max = max_l Hamiltonian^(l)
        
        # Update value function (explicit Euler):
        v(x, t) = v(x, t + Δt) + Δt * H_max
    
    # Re-initialize level set function (optional, for numerical stability):
    v ← signed_distance_reinitialization(v)

# Output: 4D array v(x, t)
```

Numerical considerations:

· Grid resolution: N = 50\text{–}100 per dimension is computationally feasible for 4D on modern hardware with GPU acceleration.
· Adaptive refinement: Regions near the viability boundary (where v \approx 0.5) require finer resolution.
· Control discretization: |\mathcal{U}| = 5\text{–}10 discrete levels per intervention dimension.

B.4 Model Predictive Control for Countermeasure Optimization

Algorithm B.5 (Receding Horizon Countermeasure Optimization).

```
Input: Current state estimate X̂(t), model parameters Θ, prediction horizon H,
       control constraints U_admissible, objective weights {w_1, w_2}
Output: Optimal control sequence {u^*(t), u^*(t+1), ..., u^*(t+H-1)}

For each MPC iteration:
    # Solve constrained optimization over prediction horizon:
    Minimize: J = Σ_{s=t}^{t+H-1} [ w_1 · ℓ(X̂(s)) + w_2 · ‖u(s)‖² ]
    Subject to:
        X̂(s+1) = discretized bilinear dynamics (Euler or Runge-Kutta)
        u(s) ∈ U_admissible
        X̂(s) ∈ K (viability constraint)
    
    # Apply first control:
    u(t) = u^*(t)
    
    # Shift horizon and repeat at next time step
```

