Appendix I: Extended Falsification Criteria

I.1 Model Comparison Tests

Test 1: Bilinear vs. Additive LTI

H_0: \mathbf{A}_j = \mathbf{0} \text{ for all } j \quad \text{(additive model is sufficient)}

H_1: \exists j: \mathbf{A}_j \neq \mathbf{0} \quad \text{(bilinear structure necessary)}

Test statistic: Likelihood ratio test:

\Lambda = 2 \left[ \mathcal{L}(\hat{\Theta}_{\text{bilinear}}) - \mathcal{L}(\hat{\Theta}_{\text{additive}}) \right] \sim \chi^2_{df}

where df = 16m (number of entries in \mathbf{A}_j matrices).

Rejection criterion: Reject H_0 if \Lambda > \chi^2_{df, 0.95}.

I.2 Viability Map Validation

Test 2: Out-of-Sample Prediction Accuracy

Split bed rest studies into training (70%) and testing (30%) sets. Fit model on training set, predict viability probabilities on testing set. Compute Brier score:

\text{Brier} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} (v(x_i, t_i) - \mathbf{1}_K(X_i(t_i)))^2

Acceptance criterion: Brier score < 0.25 (better than random guessing).

I.3 Cross-Study Generalizability

Test 3: Transfer Across Bed Rest Campaigns

Fit model on ESA RSL campaign (60-day bed rest). Apply fitted model to predict deconditioning trajectories in NASA 70-day bed rest study. Compute relative prediction error:

\text{RPE} = \frac{\|X_{\text{predicted}} - X_{\text{observed}}\|}{\|X_{\text{observed}}\|}

Acceptance criterion: Median RPE < 20% across all four state variables.

